#: community-login-idp.php:1450
msgid "Community Login"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1470
msgid "Registration"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1472
msgid "Create a new WordPress account when an unknown person signs in"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1473
msgid "Automatically link to an existing account with the same verified email address"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1474
msgid "Only enable automatic linking if you trust the provider to verify email addresses — it lets anyone controlling that email sign in as the matching WordPress user."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1478
msgid "Site visibility"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1480
msgid "Require people to be logged in to view the site"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1481
msgid "Logged-out visitors are sent to the login form. The login form itself, the provider callback, cron and the admin-ajax endpoint stay reachable, as do robots.txt and the favicon."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1484
msgid "Also require login for RSS and Atom feeds"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1485
msgid "Also require login for the REST API"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1487
msgid "Both are off by default because closing them breaks things quietly: feeds stop updating in readers, and a closed REST API stops oEmbed previews of your posts elsewhere along with any theme or plugin that reads the API without a session. Application passwords keep working either way."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1490
msgid "Always allow these paths:"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1493
msgid "One per line, matched as a prefix — /shop covers everything under it. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1497
msgid "Session length"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1500
msgid "hours"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1501
msgid "How long someone stays signed in after using a provider button. Membership of the workspace or server is only rechecked when they sign in again, so this is also how long someone keeps access after leaving your community. The default, 48 hours, matches WordPress’ own."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1505
msgid "Avatars"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1507
msgid "Use the profile picture from the provider"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1508
msgid "Images are hotlinked from Slack’s or Discord’s CDN, which tells them the IP address of every visitor who loads a page with an avatar on it — the same objection people raise about Gravatar. That is why this is off by default. Users with no linked provider, or no picture set there, keep the site’s normal avatar."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1512
msgid "Password sign-in"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1514
msgid "Disable username and password sign-in"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1516
msgid "Interactive logins must then go through a provider above. Application passwords keep working for the REST API and XML-RPC, so integrations are unaffected. Password resets are switched off too, since the resulting password could not be used."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1519
msgid "Before you enable this, link your own account to a provider."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: PHP constant definition to add to wp-config.php.
#: community-login-idp.php:1523
#, php-format
msgid "If a provider ever breaks, restore password sign-in by adding %s to wp-config.php."
msgstr ""

